## Can test with the current binary

- [ ] **P134 · Local Record persistence.** In a private workspace, save a short title, description and body edit, then reopen the Record and its dependent views. Verify the exact saved values and that a separate unsaved draft remains attached to its own Record.
- [ ] **Two-output rendering.** Show native panels and an ordinary Wayland window across the two monitors at their normal scales. Verify labels and controls stay painted and visible without blank boxes, clipping or intermittent disappearance.
- [ ] **P148 · Display preview rollback.** In Customization, preview one supported display change and let it expire. Verify the original layout and usable windows return on both monitors.
- [ ] **P104 · Laboratory report picker.** Diagnose why Load Park report opened no chooser on the installed release. Verify a real JSON/JSONL report shows its revision, results and missing measurements. If diagnosis establishes a code fix, keep only the post-fix import check in the next-binary group.

## Cannot test with the current binary alone

- [ ] **P142 · Mandatory Laboratory case.** On a compatible build, verify the Protein filter case runs through a passing report with the expected Record and rendered labels. The installed `e5f68e7b` run stopped on duplicate `PointerFocusPlugin` registration.
- [ ] **P134 R08 · Capture privacy.** With the matching private capture fixture, hold a capture across a source retirement or authorization change. Verify the pending frame exposes no retired private pixels.
- [ ] **P134 R09 · Save and recovery.** With the matching isolated crash/reopen fixture, explicitly save one IDE document, leave a separate draft, and verify the saved contents and the draft recover independently.

## Per-binary cycle

Verify the running executable's revision and profile and refill the first group with any checks the artifact now supports. Use the installed binary and any matching prebuilt fixtures. Record the revision, conditions and outcome, then remove resolved items until the runnable group is empty. Move checks that need another artifact to the second group with the specific dependency. Keep evidence outside the checklist, using commit messages or local test results without private content.

When the runnable group is empty, commit and push the scoped fixes and plan changes, then stop so the owner can get the next binary. A replacement is needed only for a remaining check with a build dependency. Preserve unrelated changes in the working tree.
